# Third-party downloaded VASP outputs (nal-hfo archive, 189 MB, 152 files).
# Not ours to redistribute; POTCAR was already excluded at extraction time.
# The scientific/workflow audit of this archive IS tracked, at
# reports/external_vasp_archive_audit_20260824/README.md
external_data/

# pytest temporary directories (distinct from .pytest_cache/)
.pytest_tmp_*/

# Generated research data. This file already lists ~24 data/ subdirectories
# individually; these four were missing, which left 588 untracked files
# (12.74 MB) reachable by `git add -A`. That included 456 files of extracted
# paper full text under data/literature_intake/**/05_fulltext/ and 301 verbatim
# publisher abstracts (abstract_snippet, up to 700 chars each) in
# data/literature/hzo_*_download_list.{csv,json}. README already bars parsed
# text from the GitHub repo. Nothing under these four paths is currently
# tracked, so ignoring them is purely additive.
# The whole-directory rule for literature_intake supersedes the granular
# **/01_papers/ .. **/04_code_and_data/ rules further up; those are left in
# place as documentation of the intake layout.
data/literature/
data/literature_intake/
data/relevance_screening/
data/unrelated_pdfs/

# Downloaded literature/data archives
*.tgz
*.tar.gz

# Licensed VASP pseudopotentials. Never commit or redistribute.
# The nal-hfo extraction already excluded all seven POTCAR members; the
# generated strain-pilot job dirs carry POTCAR_NOT_INCLUDED.txt placeholders,
# which ARE meant to be tracked - they document the deliberate omission.
POTCAR
POTCAR.*
POTCAR_*
!POTCAR_NOT_INCLUDED.txt
